#: source/advanced-topics/distributed-builds.md:1
msgid "Remote Builds"
msgstr ""

#: source/advanced-topics/distributed-builds.md:3
msgid ""
"A local Nix installation can forward Nix builds to other machines, this "
"allows multiple builds to be performed in parallel."
msgstr ""

#: source/advanced-topics/distributed-builds.md:6
msgid ""
"Remote builds also allow Nix to perform multi-platform builds in a semi-"
"transparent way. For example, if you perform a build for a `aarch64-darwin` "
"on an `i686-linux` machine, Nix can automatically forward the build to a "
"`aarch64-darwin` machine, if one is available."
msgstr ""

#: source/advanced-topics/distributed-builds.md:11
msgid "Requirements"
msgstr ""

#: source/advanced-topics/distributed-builds.md:13
msgid ""
"For a local machine to forward a build to a remote machine, the remote "
"machine must:"
msgstr ""

#: source/advanced-topics/distributed-builds.md:15
msgid "Have Nix installed"
msgstr ""

#: source/advanced-topics/distributed-builds.md:16
msgid "Be running an SSH server, e.g. `sshd`"
msgstr ""

#: source/advanced-topics/distributed-builds.md:17
msgid "Be accessible via SSH from the local machine over the network"
msgstr ""

#: source/advanced-topics/distributed-builds.md:18
msgid ""
"Have the local machine's public SSH key in `/etc/ssh/authorized_keys.d/"
"<username>`"
msgstr ""

#: source/advanced-topics/distributed-builds.md:19
msgid ""
"Have the username of the SSH user in the `trusted-users` setting in `nix."
"conf`"
msgstr ""

#: source/advanced-topics/distributed-builds.md:21
msgid "Testing"
msgstr ""

#: source/advanced-topics/distributed-builds.md:23
msgid ""
"To test connecting to a remote [Nix instance](../glossary.md#gloss-nix-"
"instance) (in this case `mac`), run:"
msgstr ""

#: source/advanced-topics/distributed-builds.md:25
msgid ""
"```console\n"
"nix store info --store ssh://username@mac\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: source/advanced-topics/distributed-builds.md:29
msgid ""
"To specify an SSH identity file as part of the remote store URI add a query "
"parameter, e.g."
msgstr ""

#: source/advanced-topics/distributed-builds.md:32
msgid ""
"```console\n"
"nix store info --store ssh://username@mac?ssh-key=/home/alice/my-key\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: source/advanced-topics/distributed-builds.md:36
msgid ""
"Since builds should be non-interactive, the key should not have a "
"passphrase. Alternatively, you can load identities ahead of time into `ssh-"
"agent` or `gpg-agent`."
msgstr ""

#: source/advanced-topics/distributed-builds.md:40
msgid ""
"In a multi-user installation (default), builds are executed by the Nix "
"Daemon. The Nix Daemon cannot prompt for a passphrase via the terminal or "
"`ssh-agent`, so the SSH key must not have a passphrase."
msgstr ""

#: source/advanced-topics/distributed-builds.md:44
msgid ""
"In addition, the Nix Daemon's user (typically root) needs to have SSH access "
"to the remote builder."
msgstr ""

#: source/advanced-topics/distributed-builds.md:47
msgid ""
"Access can be verified by running `sudo su`, and then validating SSH access, "
"e.g. by running `ssh mac`. SSH identity files for root users are usually "
"stored in `/root/.ssh/` (Linux) or `/var/root/.ssh` (MacOS)."
msgstr ""

#: source/advanced-topics/distributed-builds.md:51
msgid "If you get the error"
msgstr ""

#: source/advanced-topics/distributed-builds.md:58
msgid ""
"then you need to ensure that the `PATH` of non-interactive login shells "
"contains Nix."
msgstr ""

#: source/advanced-topics/distributed-builds.md:61
msgid ""
"The [list of remote build machines](../command-ref/conf-file.md#conf-"
"builders) can be specified on the command line or in the Nix configuration "
"file. For example, the following command allows you to build a derivation "
"for `aarch64-darwin` on a Linux machine:"
msgstr ""

#: source/advanced-topics/distributed-builds.md:72
msgid ""
"```console\n"
"nix build --impure \\\n"
" --expr '(with import <nixpkgs> { system = \"aarch64-darwin\"; }; runCommand "
"\"foo\" {} \"uname > $out\")' \\\n"
" --builders 'ssh://mac aarch64-darwin'\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: source/advanced-topics/distributed-builds.md:78
msgid ""
"```console\n"
"[1/0/1 built, 0.0 MiB DL] building foo on ssh://mac\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: source/advanced-topics/distributed-builds.md:90
msgid ""
"It is possible to specify multiple build machines separated by a semicolon "
"or a newline, e.g."
msgstr ""

#: source/advanced-topics/distributed-builds.md:92
msgid ""
"```console\n"
"  --builders 'ssh://mac aarch64-darwin ; ssh://beastie x86_64-freebsd'\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: source/advanced-topics/distributed-builds.md:96
msgid ""
"Remote build machines can also be configured in [`nix.conf`](../command-ref/"
"conf-file.md), e.g."
msgstr ""

#: source/advanced-topics/distributed-builds.md:98
msgid ""
"    builders = ssh://mac aarch64-darwin ; ssh://beastie x86_64-freebsd\n"
"    "
msgstr ""

#: source/advanced-topics/distributed-builds.md:100
msgid ""
"After making changes to `nix.conf`, restart the Nix daemon for changes to "
"take effect."
msgstr ""

#: source/advanced-topics/distributed-builds.md:102
msgid ""
"Finally, remote build machines can be configured in a separate configuration "
"file included in `builders` via the syntax `@/path/to/file`. For example,"
msgstr ""

#: source/advanced-topics/distributed-builds.md:107
msgid ""
"causes the list of machines in `/etc/nix/machines` to be included. (This is "
"the default.)"
msgstr ""
